1
00:00:12,812 --> 00:00:15,015
MICHIKO DAIMON
FREELANCE SURGEON

2
00:00:21,221 --> 00:00:22,222
Excuse me!

3
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:25,325
Please!

4
00:00:26,559 --> 00:00:29,262
- Excuse me!
- Sorry, let me pass.

5
00:00:31,331 --> 00:00:32,365
Hey.

6
00:00:32,932 --> 00:00:35,268
- Open the door.
- Please wait until 8:30.

7
00:00:39,072 --> 00:00:40,640
I'm Daimon of Surgery #2.

8
00:00:43,309 --> 00:00:45,812
You're a temp! Go to the back.

9
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:47,881
Wherever I go in is fine.

10
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:52,852
Are you okay? Hang in there!

11
00:00:52,952 --> 00:00:54,287
Are you okay?

12
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:03,563
President, please.

13
00:01:06,533 --> 00:01:08,868
<i>Mr. Nikaido is scheduled for surgery.</i>

14
00:01:09,936 --> 00:01:11,938
<i>Please take good care of him.</i>

15
00:01:12,872 --> 00:01:15,842
Yes. Since he's here on your referral,

16
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:18,445
we will do our very best.

17
00:01:18,511 --> 00:01:19,579
RYUNOSUKE BUSUJIMA
HOSPITAL CHIEF

18
00:01:19,646 --> 00:01:20,480
Thank you.

19
00:01:24,284 --> 00:01:26,953
It's as you heard.
Treat him with the utmost courtesy.

20
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:31,825
TAKASHI TORII
#2 SURGERY CHIEF - PROFESSOR

21
00:01:32,859 --> 00:01:36,830
We've received a referral
from Diet member Tanizawa

22
00:01:36,963 --> 00:01:41,101
to admit Mr. Noboru Nikaido,
the President of Nikaido Publishing House.

23
00:01:41,167 --> 00:01:43,470
- Yes. Certainly. Understood.
- Certainly.

24
00:01:43,536 --> 00:01:46,139
Oh my!
He'll be here first thing in the morning.

25
00:01:52,846 --> 00:01:54,814
Chief, at the next academic conference,

26
00:01:54,881 --> 00:01:56,749
I'd like to present my paper
on K-RAS genet--

27
00:01:56,816 --> 00:01:59,519
Please take good care of Mr. Nikaido.

28
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:07,494
Certainly.

29
00:02:15,502 --> 00:02:17,737
- We can't open until 8:30.
- Why?

30
00:02:18,071 --> 00:02:19,639
- It's a rule.
- So, why?

31
00:02:19,706 --> 00:02:20,707
It's a rule.

32
00:02:21,407 --> 00:02:23,977
Excuse me, please clear the way.
Please clear the way.

33
00:02:24,711 --> 00:02:26,346
- President, this way please.
- Good morning.

34
00:02:26,412 --> 00:02:28,748
Hey! Go to the end of the line.

35
00:02:29,949 --> 00:02:32,919
Everyone's been waiting here
for more than an hour.

36
00:02:33,019 --> 00:02:35,288
Do you know who I am?

37
00:02:35,889 --> 00:02:36,756
Who?

38
00:02:42,896 --> 00:02:44,430
You're a rude woman.

39
00:02:48,401 --> 00:02:49,369
Get on this!

40
00:02:49,435 --> 00:02:52,038
- Hey, that's mine!
- Mr. Nikaido, Mr. Nikaido!

41
00:02:56,609 --> 00:02:59,379
Mr. Nikaido, we've been waiting
for you. Please.

42
00:02:59,746 --> 00:03:01,648
What happened to the rule?

43
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:04,751
Doctor...

44
00:03:04,817 --> 00:03:06,052
- We're taking him in.
- Yes!

45
00:03:06,119 --> 00:03:06,953
Hurry!

46
00:03:15,895 --> 00:03:17,030
That's mine...

47
00:03:17,130 --> 00:03:19,666
It's okay, we'll bring you a better one.

48
00:03:20,667 --> 00:03:23,870
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

49
00:03:24,904 --> 00:03:27,574
<i>University hospitals were becoming weaker,</i>

50
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:30,076
<i>and even medicine, which deals with life,</i>

51
00:03:30,143 --> 00:03:32,845
<i>has already entered the era</i>
<i>of the law of the jungle.</i>

52
00:03:33,646 --> 00:03:37,650
<i>To fill this critical shortage</i>
<i>in the medical field, freelance,</i>

53
00:03:39,953 --> 00:03:42,922
<i>in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors, have emerged.</i>

54
00:03:45,124 --> 00:03:47,126
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

55
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:50,230
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority,</i>

56
00:03:50,296 --> 00:03:51,798
<i>and she hates restraints.</i>

57
00:03:52,031 --> 00:03:56,169
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

58
00:03:56,302 --> 00:04:00,573
Respiratory condition is stable.
No indications of pneumothorax.

59
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:03,176
It's okay. We'll examine you soon.

60
00:04:03,543 --> 00:04:05,845
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

61
00:04:06,512 --> 00:04:07,614
<i>Also known as...</i>

62
00:04:08,514 --> 00:04:09,749
<i>Doctor X.</i>

63
00:04:18,891 --> 00:04:21,761
DOCTOR X SURGEON MICHIKO DAIMON
EPISODE 2

64
00:04:40,647 --> 00:04:45,018
Compared to the previous year,
hospital stays are longer

65
00:04:45,084 --> 00:04:48,921
and the general ward turnover rate
is declining.

66
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:51,157
Deficits are soaring.

67
00:04:51,724 --> 00:04:53,359
What do you think, Manager?

68
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:55,962
I humbly apologize.

69
00:04:56,029 --> 00:04:59,999
The entire staff will...
strive to reduce costs

70
00:05:00,066 --> 00:05:03,036
and we will put ourselves
in our patients' shoes...

71
00:05:03,102 --> 00:05:04,404
KANEKO TERAYAMA
MANAGER

72
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:06,072
...to strive to create
a comfortable ward--

73
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:07,874
A hospital isn't a hotel!

74
00:05:08,708 --> 00:05:11,978
At this rate, the main hospital,
which is covering us,

75
00:05:12,211 --> 00:05:13,446
will suffer as well!

76
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:15,014
Yes.

77
00:05:15,948 --> 00:05:20,420
<i>I heard Professor Busujima was the top</i>
<i>Chief candidate for the main hospital.</i>

78
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:22,822
I wonder why a top member
of the Totei Faction...

79
00:05:22,889 --> 00:05:24,490
MAMORU HARA
#2 SURGERY - ASSISTANT PROFESSOR

80
00:05:24,557 --> 00:05:26,993
...fell from grace to a colony like ours.

81
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:29,062
He probably got in trouble.

82
00:05:29,429 --> 00:05:31,898
It could be money, women, or...

83
00:05:32,365 --> 00:05:33,599
A medical mistake?

84
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:35,335
The one who got screwed
is our Chief Surgeon.

85
00:05:35,401 --> 00:05:36,402
HIDEKI KAJI
#2 SURGERY - TEACHER

86
00:05:36,502 --> 00:05:39,238
I'm sure he wanted the new Chief's seat.

87
00:05:39,305 --> 00:05:41,841
Is that why Professor Torii is so grumpy?

88
00:05:42,241 --> 00:05:44,243
- Good morning.
- Morning.

89
00:05:44,977 --> 00:05:46,846
Why at a busy time like this?

90
00:05:46,913 --> 00:05:48,448
Professor, what's wrong?

91
00:05:48,514 --> 00:05:52,118
Mr. Nikaido, the suite room patient,
is Chief Busujima's special patient.

92
00:05:52,251 --> 00:05:53,820
Oh, first VIP in a while!

93
00:05:53,886 --> 00:05:56,556
Don't joke!
Doctors aren't a service industry.

94
00:05:56,789 --> 00:05:59,158
I'm busy with research and other things.

95
00:05:59,225 --> 00:06:00,426
You're absolutely right.

96
00:06:00,493 --> 00:06:02,562
- Professor, have some coffee.
- Okay.

97
00:06:03,329 --> 00:06:05,598
Can I ask you to pay
this month's office fund?

98
00:06:05,665 --> 00:06:06,866
I have no money now.

99
00:06:08,434 --> 00:06:10,970
- Is there no sugar or cream in here?
- Sorry.

100
00:06:16,008 --> 00:06:17,944
So much sugar is bad for you.

101
00:06:18,010 --> 00:06:21,447
It's fine.
The worst thing for your body is stress.

102
00:06:22,482 --> 00:06:24,584
Stress? Kaji, what do you mean?

103
00:06:25,284 --> 00:06:26,119
Nothing.

104
00:06:27,987 --> 00:06:29,589
- Good morning!
- Morning!

105
00:06:29,689 --> 00:06:31,691
Ah, Professor, good morning.

106
00:06:31,791 --> 00:06:34,560
Here's yesterday's gene analysis results
related to colorectal cancer

107
00:06:34,627 --> 00:06:36,562
with indication of tolerance
to anti-cancer drugs.

108
00:06:36,696 --> 00:06:37,997
Thanks for your hard work!

109
00:06:38,698 --> 00:06:40,466
I've wanted to ask you, but...

110
00:06:40,867 --> 00:06:41,868
A question? What?

111
00:06:42,335 --> 00:06:44,470
I'm confident my presentation
on K-RAS genetic mutation

112
00:06:44,537 --> 00:06:46,806
will be the highlight
at the upcoming conference.

113
00:06:46,873 --> 00:06:48,107
Ask me anything.

114
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:49,809
It's not about research, but...

115
00:06:50,276 --> 00:06:52,245
Dr. Daimon, who was fired before,
did you re-hire her?

116
00:06:52,311 --> 00:06:53,312
HIKARU MORIMOTO
#2 SURGERY - ASSISTANT

117
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:55,214
I know nothing.

118
00:06:57,784 --> 00:07:00,119
If Professor Torii didn't, who did?

119
00:07:00,186 --> 00:07:02,822
- It seems Chief Busujima did.
- What?

120
00:07:03,156 --> 00:07:05,992
That woman's already
on the Director's good side?

121
00:07:06,058 --> 00:07:08,060
You have to watch her constantly.

122
00:07:14,834 --> 00:07:17,537
Daimon, you're already late
on your first day?

123
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:20,506
I transported a critical-care patient
to emergency.

124
00:07:21,340 --> 00:07:22,708
What's that attitude?

125
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:24,677
Morimoto,

126
00:07:25,912 --> 00:07:28,681
aren't you glad
you finally have an assistant?

127
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:32,685
From now on, assisting
the Professor's research as a newcomer...

128
00:07:33,319 --> 00:07:34,320
is your job.

129
00:07:35,621 --> 00:07:36,656
I won't.

130
00:07:37,356 --> 00:07:38,257
What'd you say?

131
00:07:39,258 --> 00:07:42,028
I would like to re-confirm
my working conditions

132
00:07:42,094 --> 00:07:43,563
in front of everyone.

133
00:07:54,407 --> 00:07:55,608
Read this.

134
00:07:57,043 --> 00:07:58,778
Right here! Read it out loud.

135
00:08:00,746 --> 00:08:03,216
Helping a professor with his research.

136
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:04,917
Doing research for essays...

137
00:08:05,017 --> 00:08:05,852
I won't.

138
00:08:06,385 --> 00:08:09,288
Chief's rounds. Professor's rounds.

139
00:08:09,355 --> 00:08:10,189
I won't.

140
00:08:10,256 --> 00:08:11,591
Accompany at academic conferences.

141
00:08:11,724 --> 00:08:12,592
I won't.

142
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:13,960
Chauffeur for golf courses.

143
00:08:14,026 --> 00:08:16,229
- I won't.
- Scheme to cover up for a mistress.

144
00:08:16,295 --> 00:08:17,196
I won't.

145
00:08:17,263 --> 00:08:18,831
- Shut up!
- Et cetera, et cetera.

146
00:08:18,898 --> 00:08:21,868
I won't do anything that can't be done
without a medical license.

147
00:08:24,704 --> 00:08:26,939
Oh, please pay the office fund.

148
00:08:27,773 --> 00:08:28,741
I won't pay.

149
00:08:29,809 --> 00:08:32,578
That coffee comes
from the office fund as well.

150
00:08:37,817 --> 00:08:39,318
Then I won't drink it.

151
00:08:43,923 --> 00:08:47,527
Mr. Nikaido in the suite room
is asking for the Surgery Chief.

152
00:08:48,461 --> 00:08:49,295
Hurry!

153
00:08:49,929 --> 00:08:52,565
- Seriously, these people.
- Hurry!

154
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:56,135
It's taking so long...

155
00:08:56,202 --> 00:09:00,106
- Mr. Nikaido, how are you feeling?
- I'm fine, fine! I'm doing well.

156
00:09:00,339 --> 00:09:04,043
What? I have enough flowers until I die.

157
00:09:04,110 --> 00:09:04,977
Professor...

158
00:09:06,078 --> 00:09:09,916
Mr. Nikaido, please turn off
your cell phone when in the hospital.

159
00:09:09,982 --> 00:09:11,584
It's an important business call.

160
00:09:11,784 --> 00:09:14,320
Yeah, and... huh?
Just talking to myself.

161
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:15,755
NOBORU NIKAIDO
NIKAIDO PUBLISHING - PRESIDENT

162
00:09:15,821 --> 00:09:17,890
So come and see me
with a bottle of champagne.

163
00:09:18,357 --> 00:09:20,593
Ginza. Gin... Hey! Gin...

164
00:09:21,761 --> 00:09:23,329
Mr. Nikaido, please stop.

165
00:09:23,496 --> 00:09:24,864
SONOKO CHIBA
CHIEF NURSE

166
00:09:24,931 --> 00:09:27,733
There's an area on the 1st floor
where you can use your cell phone.

167
00:09:29,702 --> 00:09:32,104
Hey! Is this hospital making

168
00:09:32,171 --> 00:09:34,006
a gravely ill patient walk
to the 1st floor?

169
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:36,509
I'll write about it in our magazine.

170
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:39,111
Oh, one more thing. Hey!

171
00:09:39,612 --> 00:09:42,815
As you can see, I know a lot of people
in the entertainment industry.

172
00:09:43,115 --> 00:09:46,852
If I need to, I can have a news show
pick this story up as well.

173
00:09:48,387 --> 00:09:51,958
President Nikaido, not that!
Please spare us.

174
00:09:52,024 --> 00:09:55,695
Please. You may have a party
or whatever you like in this room!

175
00:09:56,562 --> 00:10:01,000
And, I'm pretty busy now, so...

176
00:10:01,367 --> 00:10:02,501
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

177
00:10:02,768 --> 00:10:05,071
Can you move up the surgery a few days?

178
00:10:05,738 --> 00:10:07,807
No, that's not possible.

179
00:10:08,074 --> 00:10:10,443
The operations are fully booked
for this week.

180
00:10:10,509 --> 00:10:12,111
It's no use talking to you.

181
00:10:13,045 --> 00:10:14,180
Call the Director.

182
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:16,115
Ah, yes.

183
00:10:18,351 --> 00:10:20,519
We will begin this week's
pre-operation conference.

184
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,021
PRE-OPERATION CONFERENCE

185
00:10:22,088 --> 00:10:24,824
The first case is Noboru Nikaido,
50 years old.

186
00:10:25,224 --> 00:10:30,029
As he is a top priority patient,
the surgery was moved up to Thursday.

187
00:10:30,262 --> 00:10:32,598
Top priority. Why?

188
00:10:32,798 --> 00:10:35,601
He's President Nikaido
of the Nikaido Publishing House.

189
00:10:36,068 --> 00:10:39,071
He was referred to us
by the honorable Diet member,

190
00:10:39,572 --> 00:10:41,841
so treat him with the utmost respect.

191
00:10:43,542 --> 00:10:44,844
You're a rude woman.

192
00:10:47,780 --> 00:10:48,681
That guy.

193
00:10:49,915 --> 00:10:51,484
Wait your turn in line.

194
00:10:58,290 --> 00:10:59,892
Who's going to be primary surgeon?

195
00:11:00,926 --> 00:11:03,229
I'd do it if I didn't have
the demonstration surgery.

196
00:11:03,963 --> 00:11:05,564
I will be the primary surgeon.

197
00:11:06,399 --> 00:11:08,234
First, the patient's condition.

198
00:11:16,409 --> 00:11:17,643
The diagnosis is pancreatic cancer

199
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:19,311
with a 5 centimeter tumor
on the pancreatic head.

200
00:11:19,378 --> 00:11:22,448
Therefore, a pancreatoduodenectomy
will be performed.

201
00:11:22,515 --> 00:11:23,516
PANCREATODUODENECTOMY

202
00:11:23,582 --> 00:11:25,117
I ask for your cooperation.

203
00:11:25,184 --> 00:11:26,285
Wait a minute.

204
00:11:27,687 --> 00:11:28,921
What if the cancer has invaded

205
00:11:28,988 --> 00:11:30,189
the superior mesenteric artery
or portal vein?

206
00:11:30,289 --> 00:11:31,290
SUPERIOR MESENTERIC ARTERY
PORTAL VEIN

207
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:33,025
Even in that case,
the procedure won't change.

208
00:11:33,492 --> 00:11:35,828
We will remove as much cancer as possible
around the blood vessels.

209
00:11:35,895 --> 00:11:38,664
After surgery, we aim
for a complete cure with chemotherapy.

210
00:11:38,731 --> 00:11:39,732
I disagree.

211
00:11:39,799 --> 00:11:42,668
Even if you resect affected organs,
cancer will recur.

212
00:11:42,835 --> 00:11:44,970
That's why I said
we'll treat with chemotherapy.

213
00:11:45,137 --> 00:11:47,306
Why not remove
the affected arteries as well?

214
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:48,474
That's crazy.

215
00:11:49,141 --> 00:11:50,643
It's common knowledge for surgeons

216
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:52,611
not to touch
the superior mesenteric artery.

217
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:55,481
I can do it.

218
00:11:57,583 --> 00:11:58,651
HIROMI JONOUCHI
ANESTHESIOLOGIST

219
00:11:59,785 --> 00:12:01,854
She's probably after the VIP's tip.

220
00:12:02,455 --> 00:12:05,024
Nikaido Publishing House
also publishes medical journals.

221
00:12:05,257 --> 00:12:07,193
She's definitely after money or publicity.

222
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:10,463
She's an absolute disgrace to surgeons.

223
00:12:11,597 --> 00:12:14,300
You perform the surgery on the VIP?
Are you serious?

224
00:12:14,366 --> 00:12:16,936
- Of course.
- What're you saying, like you know it all?

225
00:12:17,203 --> 00:12:20,406
There's no way we'd entrust
a VIP's surgery to an outsider like you.

226
00:12:20,473 --> 00:12:21,540
That's right.

227
00:12:21,607 --> 00:12:25,411
If you fail, the good name
of this hospital will be ruined.

228
00:12:25,478 --> 00:12:26,846
It's okay if I don't fail, yes?

229
00:12:27,613 --> 00:12:28,514
What'd you say?

230
00:12:30,116 --> 00:12:33,018
I will not fail.

231
00:12:39,225 --> 00:12:40,826
Let me do the surgery.

232
00:12:42,061 --> 00:12:43,596
- No.
- Why?

233
00:12:44,964 --> 00:12:49,835
Anyways, the surgery I was originally
scheduled to do will be done next week.

234
00:12:51,537 --> 00:12:52,772
How about...

235
00:12:53,606 --> 00:12:56,375
we give that surgery to Dr. Daimon?

236
00:12:57,977 --> 00:13:00,479
As I recall, that's also a case
with pancreatic cancer.

237
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:01,647
But...

238
00:13:03,215 --> 00:13:05,718
Daimon... what do you think?

239
00:13:08,387 --> 00:13:10,222
You will not fail, right?

240
00:13:15,127 --> 00:13:15,961
Yes.

241
00:13:16,028 --> 00:13:17,630
Well then, let's continue.

242
00:13:18,063 --> 00:13:20,900
The next case is Mr. Satoshi Yasuda.
Pancreatic cancer.

243
00:13:21,667 --> 00:13:24,203
There's an 8 centimeter tumor
on the pancreatic head...

244
00:13:31,510 --> 00:13:36,115
That's tough. If Mr. Torii's operating,
a life that can be saved might be lost.

245
00:13:36,182 --> 00:13:38,617
I feel bad for the VIP patient.

246
00:13:38,684 --> 00:13:41,287
Is Professor Torii that bad?

247
00:13:41,353 --> 00:13:43,789
Well, more like he really sucks.

248
00:13:44,757 --> 00:13:46,492
Even though he's a professor?

249
00:13:46,959 --> 00:13:51,297
He's a bookworm who became a professor
with research, papers and lobbying.

250
00:13:51,430 --> 00:13:53,332
His surgical skills are intern level.

251
00:13:53,799 --> 00:13:55,734
That bad, huh?

252
00:13:55,801 --> 00:13:59,138
But still,
he has to do at least one surgery a month

253
00:13:59,572 --> 00:14:03,008
to preserve his face and appearance
as Chief Surgeon.

254
00:14:03,209 --> 00:14:05,978
To get killed for the sake
of face and appearance is awful.

255
00:14:06,045 --> 00:14:07,346
Michiko, mind your own business.

256
00:14:07,413 --> 00:14:08,414
AKIRA KAMBARA
DOCTOR REFERRAL SERVICE CHIEF

257
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:10,549
If you get involved,
you'll be fired again.

258
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:12,084
<i>Riichi.</i>

259
00:14:13,385 --> 00:14:15,688
Medical offices in university hospitals

260
00:14:16,288 --> 00:14:18,891
are built on useless principles

261
00:14:18,958 --> 00:14:21,827
like titles, authority,
face and appearance.

262
00:14:22,061 --> 00:14:24,864
Without them,
the ivory tower will crumble.

263
00:14:24,997 --> 00:14:26,632
That's what it's about.

264
00:14:32,938 --> 00:14:35,107
Michiko. <i>Ron.</i>

265
00:14:38,110 --> 00:14:40,179
<i>Riichi ippatsu.</i>

266
00:14:40,246 --> 00:14:41,814
<i>Junchan sanshoku.</i>

267
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:43,816
<i>Dora dora no baiman.</i>

268
00:14:49,121 --> 00:14:54,126
<i>From now, Professor Busujima will now make</i>
<i>the Director's rounds of the surgery ward.</i>

269
00:15:05,404 --> 00:15:06,238
Mr. Nikaido.

270
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:10,509
- Tomorrow is the operation.
- Yes.

271
00:15:12,244 --> 00:15:16,115
Professor Torii, who is considered
a pancreatic expert, is your main surgeon,

272
00:15:16,315 --> 00:15:18,517
so please be at ease and leave it to him.

273
00:15:20,386 --> 00:15:22,388
Doctor, I'm counting on you.

274
00:15:24,723 --> 00:15:26,725
- Kusakabe, give me that.
- Yes, sir.

275
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:31,096
Here.

276
00:15:31,597 --> 00:15:33,198
Doctor, please accept this.

277
00:15:34,266 --> 00:15:37,202
No, we can't accept that.

278
00:15:37,870 --> 00:15:39,772
- Please, put it away.
- Huh?

279
00:15:47,913 --> 00:15:49,581
Mr. Yasuda, what's your job?

280
00:15:50,416 --> 00:15:52,985
I'm unemployed right now.
The company went bankrupt.

281
00:15:53,052 --> 00:15:55,854
How long have you felt discomfort
in your back?

282
00:15:56,855 --> 00:16:00,826
Let's see, it's been about three months.

283
00:16:01,727 --> 00:16:06,031
It didn't hurt that badly, so I thought
I strained a muscle or something.

284
00:16:06,732 --> 00:16:09,835
Well, please refrain
from eating until dinner

285
00:16:09,902 --> 00:16:11,670
and no fluids after 9:00 p.m.

286
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:16,809
Um... are you going to do the surgery
and not Professor Torii?

287
00:16:16,875 --> 00:16:17,743
Yes.

288
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:19,445
There's been a change
and I'll be doing it.

289
00:16:21,413 --> 00:16:25,184
I should have known an elite professor
wouldn't do a surgery on someone like me.

290
00:16:26,051 --> 00:16:28,854
- You may be luckier than you know.
- What?

291
00:16:29,355 --> 00:16:31,824
The Director will be
making his rounds shortly.

292
00:16:31,890 --> 00:16:33,892
Please clean up around the beds.

293
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:37,863
He's already in the next room,
open the front and please wait.

294
00:16:38,330 --> 00:16:39,331
What's going on?

295
00:16:39,398 --> 00:16:41,667
Well, Mr. Yasuda,
let's go to the examination room.

296
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:44,103
- What about the Chi--
- It's okay, let's go.

297
00:16:44,169 --> 00:16:45,037
Okay.

298
00:16:47,339 --> 00:16:49,174
- Out of the way.
- Can't you see?

299
00:16:49,241 --> 00:16:51,010
We're going to the examination room.

300
00:16:53,946 --> 00:16:54,780
Daimon.

301
00:16:57,483 --> 00:16:59,918
Doctor, why aren't you
with the other doctors?

302
00:16:59,985 --> 00:17:01,820
I won't do any useless tasks.

303
00:17:02,388 --> 00:17:03,222
Useless?

304
00:17:03,322 --> 00:17:07,092
Even extras without a medical license
can be attendants in a procession.

305
00:17:07,159 --> 00:17:09,361
It's troublesome for patients, too.

306
00:17:10,662 --> 00:17:13,899
I'm terribly sorry.
I will reprimand her severely later.

307
00:17:17,836 --> 00:17:21,140
That's all for the devices to be prepared.
Thank you.

308
00:17:21,473 --> 00:17:24,510
Mr. Yasuda has no problems
with medical history,

309
00:17:24,576 --> 00:17:25,944
complications or allergies.

310
00:17:26,011 --> 00:17:27,112
That's right.

311
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:32,151
I was told by the professor to assist you
with Mr. Yasuda's surgery tomorrow.

312
00:17:37,489 --> 00:17:41,060
That's the CT for Mr. Nikaido,
who Professor Torii is operating on.

313
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:43,829
This one has higher priority.

314
00:17:44,930 --> 00:17:46,665
What do you mean by priority?

315
00:17:47,132 --> 00:17:51,403
Does she want the VIP's tip that badly?

316
00:17:52,304 --> 00:17:55,074
Life shouldn't be measured
by wealth or poverty.

317
00:17:56,942 --> 00:17:57,943
Daimon.

318
00:17:58,610 --> 00:18:02,247
I heard you made some ridiculous comments
when the Director made his rounds.

319
00:18:02,381 --> 00:18:04,016
Like "useless" and "bothersome."

320
00:18:04,316 --> 00:18:08,587
You know nothing.
All the patients love the Chief's rounds.

321
00:18:10,389 --> 00:18:11,223
Why?

322
00:18:11,290 --> 00:18:15,828
It's because they actually feel like
they are being examined by the Chief.

323
00:18:16,462 --> 00:18:18,030
- Certainly.
- Certainly.

324
00:18:19,064 --> 00:18:20,432
Hey. Are you listening?

325
00:18:20,499 --> 00:18:21,600
I can hear you.

326
00:18:21,667 --> 00:18:23,669
You keep saying "certainly."
What language is that?

327
00:18:23,735 --> 00:18:25,938
- It's Japanese, of course.
- Certainly.

328
00:18:26,638 --> 00:18:27,739
What are you looking at?

329
00:18:30,676 --> 00:18:33,145
Tomorrow's operation.
We should switch after all.

330
00:18:33,212 --> 00:18:35,314
I'll do this one, please do Mr. Yasuda's.

331
00:18:35,781 --> 00:18:37,249
I don't get what you're saying.

332
00:18:37,716 --> 00:18:41,587
Why do I, a professor, have to take orders
from a freelancer like you?

333
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:44,056
Indeed!

334
00:18:46,391 --> 00:18:47,493
But...

335
00:18:49,995 --> 00:18:51,830
you suck at surgery, right?

336
00:18:57,769 --> 00:18:59,138
Shut your mouth!

337
00:19:08,447 --> 00:19:13,552
Complications such as pancreatic fistula,
peritonitis, infection, thrombosis,

338
00:19:14,186 --> 00:19:17,322
pulmonary and/or cardiac complications,
intestinal obstruction

339
00:19:17,456 --> 00:19:19,892
and post-operative bleeding may occur.

340
00:19:20,225 --> 00:19:22,194
That's all. Do you have any questions?

341
00:19:23,328 --> 00:19:26,098
The operation... how long will it take?

342
00:19:26,565 --> 00:19:28,333
We're planning on three hours.

343
00:19:29,134 --> 00:19:32,638
Then, if you would sign this consent form.

344
00:19:39,678 --> 00:19:42,047
- I might change my mind after all!
- Dear!

345
00:19:42,981 --> 00:19:45,083
I got scared
after hearing the explanation.

346
00:19:45,150 --> 00:19:49,021
You're saying it's a major operation
and it could be life-threatening, right?

347
00:19:49,321 --> 00:19:52,624
Then why bother getting cut open
and having that pain?

348
00:19:53,091 --> 00:19:57,496
I understand your fear after hearing all
about the surgery and complication risks,

349
00:19:57,563 --> 00:19:59,298
but we will do our best.

350
00:20:00,332 --> 00:20:01,967
If you don't have the surgery, you'll die.

351
00:20:02,034 --> 00:20:02,901
What?

352
00:20:03,669 --> 00:20:04,836
Dr. Daimon!

353
00:20:05,571 --> 00:20:08,240
But the operation might fail too, right?

354
00:20:08,874 --> 00:20:10,943
Even if it fails, you'll die.

355
00:20:16,315 --> 00:20:17,549
But I won't let you die.

356
00:20:19,685 --> 00:20:21,253
I will never fail.

357
00:20:31,096 --> 00:20:34,066
I understand. I'm counting on you!

358
00:20:39,738 --> 00:20:43,508
Doctor! Please save my husband! Please!

359
00:20:44,276 --> 00:20:46,645
Um, hospital rules prohibit us
from accepting tips.

360
00:20:46,712 --> 00:20:48,547
Please don't worry and take it.

361
00:20:51,817 --> 00:20:52,884
If you'll excuse me.

362
00:20:54,219 --> 00:20:56,622
Wait, Dr. Daimon!
We haven't discussed tomorrow's...

363
00:21:13,505 --> 00:21:15,173
<i>I knew she wasn't human.</i>

364
00:21:16,308 --> 00:21:17,276
She's a demon.

365
00:21:19,745 --> 00:21:24,816
Did she tell the patient
"I will never fail" with a smug look?

366
00:21:26,018 --> 00:21:27,753
- She did.
- What?

367
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:31,256
Even more,
she accepted the tip right there.

368
00:21:31,323 --> 00:21:35,093
What? She should at least
follow formalities and say no once.

369
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:36,161
What?

370
00:21:38,864 --> 00:21:40,999
No, anyways, it's really bad.

371
00:21:41,066 --> 00:21:47,005
Right. Here I spent a long time explaining
the risks so we don't get sued...

372
00:21:47,239 --> 00:21:49,474
It's amazing she hasn't been sued yet.

373
00:21:49,641 --> 00:21:51,943
She's probably being sued everywhere.

374
00:21:52,611 --> 00:21:53,945
That's why she needs money.

375
00:22:07,092 --> 00:22:09,061
AI OKUMURA
DR. TORII'S SECRETARY

376
00:22:09,127 --> 00:22:11,830
- You can go home first.
- What?

377
00:22:12,964 --> 00:22:15,867
Professor, the surgery came
at the right time, no?

378
00:22:17,002 --> 00:22:19,738
Nikaido Publishing publishes
lots of magazines.

379
00:22:19,805 --> 00:22:23,308
If the surgery goes well,
I'm sure they'll write a profile of you!

380
00:22:25,610 --> 00:22:26,511
For both you,

381
00:22:28,146 --> 00:22:29,247
and the hospital,

382
00:22:29,715 --> 00:22:31,316
it'll be good publicity.

383
00:22:32,250 --> 00:22:34,553
If the operation goes well,
I'll buy you something.

384
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:35,954
I'm glad.

385
00:22:36,755 --> 00:22:38,924
A new bag would be nice.

386
00:22:39,091 --> 00:22:42,461
- A new bag again?
- I don't want to lose to Michiko Daimon.

387
00:22:42,661 --> 00:22:45,397
She got a brand new one again.

388
00:22:45,464 --> 00:22:46,431
I got it.

389
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:49,568
See you.

390
00:22:58,310 --> 00:23:00,078
What if the cancer has invaded

391
00:23:00,145 --> 00:23:01,546
the superior mesenteric artery
or portal vein?

392
00:23:04,049 --> 00:23:05,751
Why not remove the affected arteries too?

393
00:23:07,452 --> 00:23:09,020
I can do it.

394
00:23:10,756 --> 00:23:12,758
You suck at surgery, right?

395
00:23:18,196 --> 00:23:19,931
- I'm back.
- Hey.

396
00:23:20,265 --> 00:23:22,501
Didn't you go dancing tonight? Wanna play?

397
00:23:22,567 --> 00:23:25,537
Nope. I might have a long day tomorrow.

398
00:23:25,604 --> 00:23:27,706
Hey. Let's play one game at least.

399
00:23:28,173 --> 00:23:29,608
I have things to do.

400
00:23:29,674 --> 00:23:30,709
Things to do?

401
00:23:31,743 --> 00:23:32,844
Like what?

402
00:23:32,911 --> 00:23:35,247
She says she loves surgery the most.

403
00:23:35,714 --> 00:23:39,651
That's why men never get near her.
Right, Casey?

404
00:23:49,060 --> 00:23:52,197
I see. You also have
pancreatic cancer surgery today.

405
00:23:52,664 --> 00:23:53,498
Yes.

406
00:23:54,332 --> 00:23:56,034
Well, good luck.

407
00:24:09,748 --> 00:24:11,983
Blood pressure is 125 over 70.

408
00:24:12,617 --> 00:24:13,919
No problems in particular.

409
00:24:17,589 --> 00:24:18,457
Where is it?

410
00:24:21,193 --> 00:24:22,060
The music?

411
00:24:22,527 --> 00:24:23,895
No. That.

412
00:24:25,831 --> 00:24:26,665
Excuse me.

413
00:24:29,701 --> 00:24:30,702
Excuse me.

414
00:24:31,903 --> 00:24:34,539
PROFESSOR TORII

415
00:24:35,774 --> 00:24:36,875
Okay, let's begin.

416
00:24:37,509 --> 00:24:40,412
We will now begin Mr. Noboru Nikaido's

417
00:24:40,579 --> 00:24:43,014
pancreatoduodenectomy surgery
by Professor Torii.

418
00:24:43,081 --> 00:24:44,749
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

419
00:24:44,816 --> 00:24:45,650
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

420
00:24:45,717 --> 00:24:49,254
OPERATION ROOM #1
PROFESSOR TORII OPERATION START 11:15 A.M.

421
00:24:49,688 --> 00:24:50,755
- Monopolar.
- Yes.

422
00:24:54,059 --> 00:24:57,095
- Is he going to be okay?
- Uh, what?

423
00:24:58,096 --> 00:25:00,932
This is the first time
I've seen him operate.

424
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:03,034
Is that so?

425
00:25:03,101 --> 00:25:06,738
Professor Torii is
definitely fired up today.

426
00:25:22,020 --> 00:25:25,357
Under epidural and general anesthesia.
Vitals are stable.

427
00:25:25,423 --> 00:25:26,525
Let's begin.

428
00:25:26,992 --> 00:25:28,326
Shall I play music?

429
00:25:28,393 --> 00:25:31,029
It's going to be three hours,
so it's better to rel--

430
00:25:31,096 --> 00:25:33,632
- I don't need it. We're going quickly.
- Yes.

431
00:25:33,865 --> 00:25:34,833
From now we will begin

432
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:37,669
Mr. Satoshi Yasuda's
pancreatoduodenectomy surgery...

433
00:25:43,041 --> 00:25:43,909
Suction, please.

434
00:25:43,975 --> 00:25:46,411
OPERATION ROOM #4
MICHIKO DAIMON OPERATION START 11:30 A.M.

435
00:25:47,412 --> 00:25:48,513
Monopolar.

436
00:26:00,759 --> 00:26:01,593
Sweat.

437
00:26:02,427 --> 00:26:03,261
Excuse me.

438
00:26:04,262 --> 00:26:06,097
- Forceps.
- Yes.

439
00:26:08,266 --> 00:26:09,401
- Kelly!
- Yes.

440
00:26:13,238 --> 00:26:14,439
- Sweat.
- Yes.

441
00:26:15,340 --> 00:26:16,274
Sweat!

442
00:26:30,155 --> 00:26:32,324
Ah, I'll get a hold of it again.

443
00:26:32,390 --> 00:26:34,225
- What are you doing?
- Excuse me.

444
00:26:35,560 --> 00:26:36,828
- Sweat.
- Yes.

445
00:26:37,495 --> 00:26:38,330
Excuse me.

446
00:26:39,097 --> 00:26:41,600
- Not me, him.
- Yes.

447
00:26:57,415 --> 00:27:00,652
All right. I can see the SMA.

448
00:27:08,059 --> 00:27:08,994
It can't be!

449
00:27:09,694 --> 00:27:11,863
- Professor!
- It's spread more than expected.

450
00:27:12,464 --> 00:27:14,232
The artery is entangled in the tumor.

451
00:27:16,368 --> 00:27:17,335
What should we do?

452
00:27:21,740 --> 00:27:28,246
Cancer has invaded
the superior mesenteric artery.

453
00:27:28,747 --> 00:27:29,981
That's bad...

454
00:27:31,149 --> 00:27:32,984
What'll happen with the operation?

455
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:37,455
Professor, what should we do?

456
00:27:41,826 --> 00:27:45,964
Even if we remove the cancerous tissues,
the prognosis will not change.

457
00:27:47,599 --> 00:27:50,468
It's unfortunate, but let's close up.

458
00:27:53,371 --> 00:27:55,640
He's stopping? No way...

459
00:27:56,074 --> 00:27:58,143
Do your best
and don't give up until the end!

460
00:27:58,443 --> 00:28:00,145
He's not a normal patient!

461
00:28:00,612 --> 00:28:01,913
Chief, what should we do?

462
00:28:05,016 --> 00:28:07,552
Professor Torii, this is Busujima.

463
00:28:09,521 --> 00:28:11,823
Who said it was okay to close up?

464
00:28:13,758 --> 00:28:15,593
I, the Chief, can't allow that.

465
00:28:16,661 --> 00:28:18,663
- But...
- You may not close up.

466
00:28:19,531 --> 00:28:20,665
Remove the cancer!

467
00:28:23,868 --> 00:28:25,236
Resecting the organ

468
00:28:25,804 --> 00:28:27,505
would be more difficult for the patient.

469
00:28:27,572 --> 00:28:29,974
That means all you did was open and close!

470
00:28:33,144 --> 00:28:34,512
Finish the surgery.

471
00:28:34,979 --> 00:28:36,047
No matter what.

472
00:28:36,581 --> 00:28:37,782
Until the very end!

473
00:28:51,429 --> 00:28:54,833
The tumor is bigger than expected,
but there isn't a lot of adhesion.

474
00:28:55,300 --> 00:28:57,569
- We'll go ahead and remove it. Scalpel.
- Yes.

475
00:29:05,677 --> 00:29:07,212
Hello. Operation Room #4.

476
00:29:09,481 --> 00:29:11,216
Dr. Daimon, it's the Chief.

477
00:29:11,282 --> 00:29:12,884
You take it.

478
00:29:14,319 --> 00:29:15,186
Okay.

479
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:22,627
Mosquito.

480
00:29:22,694 --> 00:29:23,561
Yes.

481
00:29:23,728 --> 00:29:27,332
Have Daimon come
to Operation Room #1 immediately.

482
00:29:29,167 --> 00:29:30,635
The doctor is performing surgery!

483
00:29:30,702 --> 00:29:32,470
Just have her come at once!

484
00:29:37,308 --> 00:29:39,711
It's impossible. It's still going
to take a while here as well.

485
00:29:43,248 --> 00:29:45,917
Chief, I'm sorry.
It will take at least two more hou--

486
00:29:46,684 --> 00:29:48,453
Chief, this is Daimon.
I'll be right there.

487
00:29:49,187 --> 00:29:51,589
- You take over here.
- Wait, please!

488
00:29:52,357 --> 00:29:54,459
Are you giving up
Mr. Yasuda's surgery halfway?

489
00:29:54,726 --> 00:29:56,661
It's the priority order. Move.

490
00:29:57,629 --> 00:29:58,630
Is that money?

491
00:30:00,365 --> 00:30:02,967
Are you giving priority to a rich patient
more than this one?

492
00:30:03,034 --> 00:30:05,870
- Is the VIP more important?
- You're an assistant, right?

493
00:30:05,937 --> 00:30:07,172
I refuse.

494
00:30:07,906 --> 00:30:10,508
You should be responsible
for the patient until the end.

495
00:30:15,246 --> 00:30:16,614
You're mistaken!

496
00:30:17,315 --> 00:30:20,218
As a surgeon and as a human,
you're the worst!

497
00:30:44,609 --> 00:30:46,678
Daimon, why are you here?

498
00:30:47,946 --> 00:30:51,482
I was called to help here,
but my assistant won't listen.

499
00:30:51,549 --> 00:30:53,251
- I'll leave the rest to you.
- What?

500
00:30:53,318 --> 00:30:56,020
- You left the other patient in the mid--
- Hurry.

501
00:31:00,325 --> 00:31:01,326
Daimon.

502
00:31:02,260 --> 00:31:03,761
I'm counting on you.

503
00:31:04,963 --> 00:31:09,200
However, let it be known
that you were never here.

504
00:31:10,435 --> 00:31:11,402
What?

505
00:31:13,972 --> 00:31:14,906
Wait!

506
00:31:17,475 --> 00:31:19,844
Chief, this is bad!

507
00:31:19,911 --> 00:31:23,281
What will you do
if Dr. Daimon's surgery doesn't succeed?

508
00:31:23,348 --> 00:31:25,917
She said she will not fail, right?

509
00:31:26,017 --> 00:31:28,920
Who will take responsibility
if something happens?

510
00:31:30,788 --> 00:31:31,990
Chief!

511
00:31:36,928 --> 00:31:39,163
As I thought. I told you so.

512
00:31:40,698 --> 00:31:42,233
Move. You're in the way.

513
00:31:50,041 --> 00:31:52,410
Since there's no one else,
Professor, you're the assistant.

514
00:31:52,810 --> 00:31:53,711
What'll you do?

515
00:31:59,817 --> 00:32:02,153
Assistant.
We're modifying the surgical field.

516
00:32:02,487 --> 00:32:04,422
- Sterilize the thigh area.
- What?

517
00:32:04,822 --> 00:32:06,925
This is for pancreatic cancer.
Why the leg?

518
00:32:06,991 --> 00:32:08,226
Assistant, hurry up and do it!

519
00:32:11,462 --> 00:32:13,965
Anesthesiologist,
administer anesthetics to the legs.

520
00:32:14,032 --> 00:32:15,867
That's impossible so suddenly.

521
00:32:15,934 --> 00:32:19,570
Change the anesthesiologist.
Get Dr. Jonouchi from Operation Room #4.

522
00:32:19,837 --> 00:32:22,874
Prepare for anastomosis, 7/0 nylon.

523
00:32:27,245 --> 00:32:29,247
Let me know
if the blood pressure goes below 70.

524
00:32:29,347 --> 00:32:30,181
Yes.

525
00:32:38,389 --> 00:32:39,490
Huh? What's wrong?

526
00:32:41,225 --> 00:32:42,961
No way, I can't believe it...

527
00:32:48,733 --> 00:32:52,136
The heart is beating and it's stable.

528
00:32:52,203 --> 00:32:53,504
Don't scare me like that!

529
00:32:54,305 --> 00:32:56,908
It's only been an hour
since surgery began.

530
00:32:58,176 --> 00:33:00,244
I thought it would take
at least three hours

531
00:33:00,311 --> 00:33:02,146
to do a distal pancreatectomy.

532
00:33:02,213 --> 00:33:05,450
She finished everything in an hour,
including the margins.

533
00:33:07,285 --> 00:33:08,886
Hemostasis is perfect, too.

534
00:33:10,254 --> 00:33:12,290
All I can say is... brilliant.

535
00:33:12,957 --> 00:33:14,492
She did all this in under an hour?

536
00:33:15,293 --> 00:33:16,127
Really?

537
00:33:18,963 --> 00:33:19,797
Yes.

538
00:33:27,538 --> 00:33:30,074
Added 10cc lidocaine to epidural.

539
00:33:30,641 --> 00:33:32,176
Anesthesia has spread to the legs.

540
00:33:32,243 --> 00:33:36,047
We will perform an en bloc resection
of the pancreatic head, including the SMA.

541
00:33:36,247 --> 00:33:39,117
First, harvest a graft
of at least 6 centimeters

542
00:33:39,183 --> 00:33:40,985
from the thigh's great saphenous vein.

543
00:33:41,252 --> 00:33:46,657
Next, resect the pancreatic head,
SMA and portal vein at the same time.

544
00:33:46,924 --> 00:33:49,660
Finally, reconstruct
both vascular transplants.

545
00:33:50,828 --> 00:33:52,897
- Let's start. Scalpel.
- Yes.

546
00:33:53,364 --> 00:33:54,399
Wait a minute.

547
00:33:55,066 --> 00:33:57,502
I've only read about
that procedure in a paper.

548
00:33:57,735 --> 00:33:59,470
There will be massive bleeding
if you fail.

549
00:34:00,838 --> 00:34:02,273
Who'll take responsibility? Not me.

550
00:34:03,207 --> 00:34:05,209
The assistant just has to do suction,
it's fine.

551
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:07,678
I will never fail.

552
00:34:09,947 --> 00:34:11,182
- Clamp.
- Yes.

553
00:34:13,985 --> 00:34:14,952
Lower the loupe.

554
00:34:18,589 --> 00:34:19,757
- Metzen.
- Yes.

555
00:34:38,476 --> 00:34:40,878
- What's the blood loss?
- 560cc.

556
00:34:41,345 --> 00:34:44,215
I sutured the blood vessels,
so watch out for bleeding from the drain.

557
00:34:44,682 --> 00:34:45,516
You do it.

558
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:48,186
No, I'm a freelancer.

559
00:34:48,886 --> 00:34:50,755
My time is up, so excuse me.

560
00:35:04,268 --> 00:35:05,570
Thank you for your hard work.

561
00:35:07,071 --> 00:35:10,842
MICHIKO DAIMON SURGERY COMPLETE 5:35 P.M.

562
00:35:26,023 --> 00:35:26,858
Chief!

563
00:35:27,458 --> 00:35:28,292
Chief!

564
00:35:28,359 --> 00:35:29,861
That manager is here again!

565
00:35:34,632 --> 00:35:36,334
VISITOR

566
00:35:36,400 --> 00:35:38,269
Yes, I've come again.

567
00:35:38,736 --> 00:35:39,670
What do you want today?

568
00:35:39,737 --> 00:35:43,141
Today's double operation will cost extra.

569
00:35:43,441 --> 00:35:45,276
I trust you'll take care of it.

570
00:35:45,343 --> 00:35:50,348
In addition, work went beyond
5:00 p.m. for 35 minutes.

571
00:35:50,848 --> 00:35:52,049
This is a melon.

572
00:35:52,350 --> 00:35:54,185
We'll give you five minutes for free,

573
00:35:54,619 --> 00:35:58,122
and round it down to 30 minutes
for the overtime charge.

574
00:35:59,857 --> 00:36:01,125
Please be at ease.

575
00:36:01,192 --> 00:36:06,664
We will never tell the patient or family
that Michiko Daimon performed the surgery.

576
00:36:07,231 --> 00:36:09,233
We will not leak that to the media either.

577
00:36:09,734 --> 00:36:12,203
We thank you for your help.

578
00:36:13,437 --> 00:36:14,472
Instead...

579
00:36:16,073 --> 00:36:18,376
with regard to the tip for the surgery,

580
00:36:19,076 --> 00:36:24,582
please think of it as hush money,
and promptly turn it over to us.

581
00:36:25,616 --> 00:36:29,587
I'm sorry, but at this hospital
we don't accept gifts such as tips.

582
00:36:29,754 --> 00:36:31,022
Really, that again?

583
00:36:32,557 --> 00:36:34,559
It doesn't require a receipt,

584
00:36:34,892 --> 00:36:36,661
and you don't pay taxes on it.

585
00:36:37,161 --> 00:36:38,629
It's all profit, right?

586
00:36:40,498 --> 00:36:43,868
Of course, that's if you actually get it.

587
00:36:59,517 --> 00:37:00,484
No way...

588
00:37:01,052 --> 00:37:03,955
Was she planning on doing
both surgeries from the start?

589
00:37:06,557 --> 00:37:07,758
No way, right?

590
00:37:10,394 --> 00:37:12,063
Maybe her priorities...

591
00:37:12,663 --> 00:37:14,332
They weren't based on money.

592
00:37:26,877 --> 00:37:28,346
Don't misunderstand.

593
00:37:30,314 --> 00:37:32,316
Things just happened to go well today.

594
00:37:33,551 --> 00:37:35,620
There's no doctor who doesn't fail.

595
00:37:48,099 --> 00:37:50,468
What should I make for lunch tomorrow?

596
00:38:18,095 --> 00:38:21,198
ONE WEEK LATER

597
00:38:21,265 --> 00:38:26,704
<i>From now, Professor Busujima</i>
<i>will make his rounds in the surgery ward.</i>

598
00:38:31,475 --> 00:38:32,510
What's up today?

599
00:38:34,211 --> 00:38:38,716
You said you don't participate
in processions, right?

600
00:38:46,390 --> 00:38:47,425
Mr. Nikaido.

601
00:38:48,292 --> 00:38:50,094
- Are you doing well?
- Yes.

602
00:38:50,528 --> 00:38:54,899
Liver function is normal, minimal drain
bleeding, and no abnormalities observed.

603
00:38:55,166 --> 00:38:56,600
You're progressing well.

604
00:38:56,934 --> 00:38:59,403
You can leave the hospital
tomorrow as planned.

605
00:38:59,470 --> 00:39:03,941
The Chief Surgeon's surgery was great,
true to your reputation.

606
00:39:04,008 --> 00:39:04,975
Not at all...

607
00:39:06,043 --> 00:39:10,514
Let me introduce Professor Torii's
divine hands in a magazine sometime soon.

608
00:39:14,552 --> 00:39:16,987
Dr. Torii, please join us.

609
00:39:20,624 --> 00:39:24,428
Chief Surgeon, get closer. Smile, smile!

610
00:39:24,628 --> 00:39:26,263
I'm in the way, right?

611
00:39:32,837 --> 00:39:34,305
Kusakabe, give me that.

612
00:39:34,805 --> 00:39:35,673
Yes.

613
00:39:38,075 --> 00:39:38,943
Here.

614
00:39:39,577 --> 00:39:42,113
Professor, thanks for your hard work.

615
00:39:44,315 --> 00:39:47,918
I can't accept this.
I merely did what a surgeon should do.

616
00:39:47,985 --> 00:39:49,653
Please don't worry about it.

617
00:39:59,697 --> 00:40:01,966
Excuse us for not knowing earlier...

618
00:40:02,633 --> 00:40:04,001
Well, if you insist.

619
00:40:04,969 --> 00:40:06,070
Excuse me.

620
00:40:07,938 --> 00:40:08,839
Take care.

621
00:40:17,982 --> 00:40:20,017
The bag. When can we buy it?

622
00:40:22,753 --> 00:40:24,555
Yes. Who is it?

623
00:40:27,825 --> 00:40:31,228
Dr. Torii, thanks as always for your help.

624
00:40:32,463 --> 00:40:33,397
A melon.

625
00:40:33,697 --> 00:40:36,167
Well, well. Have a seat.

626
00:40:36,434 --> 00:40:39,303
- I've come here to collect.
- What?

627
00:41:39,029 --> 00:41:44,969
I hear that Surgery #2 is flooded
with patients requesting Torii.

628
00:41:46,504 --> 00:41:50,174
This is what I mean
by hospital management.

629
00:41:51,842 --> 00:41:53,844
Torii is known for

630
00:41:54,578 --> 00:41:57,114
his research and papers,

631
00:41:58,182 --> 00:41:59,450
but I didn't know...

632
00:41:59,517 --> 00:42:01,151
FAMOUS PANCREATIC CANCER DOCTOR
PROFESSOR TAKASHI TORII

633
00:42:01,218 --> 00:42:02,553
...he was a good surgeon as well.

634
00:42:04,655 --> 00:42:07,525
Of course, our surgery department...

635
00:42:08,792 --> 00:42:10,160
is outstanding.

636
00:42:17,902 --> 00:42:19,737
Thank you very much.

637
00:42:20,538 --> 00:42:22,439
I'm so glad I believed in you, Doctor!

638
00:42:22,640 --> 00:42:26,544
He's such a chicken, so when he said
he didn't need surgery I was at a loss,

639
00:42:26,610 --> 00:42:27,845
so thank you very much!

640
00:42:30,514 --> 00:42:32,216
This... I don't need it.

641
00:42:33,417 --> 00:42:34,785
It's just 50,000 yen.

642
00:42:36,220 --> 00:42:38,889
I don't accept anything
less than 100,000 yen.

643
00:42:44,628 --> 00:42:47,298
Um, please eat something nutritious
with that instead.

644
00:42:47,498 --> 00:42:51,302
It's much better than giving it to someone
like her. Please excuse me. Take care.

645
00:42:52,836 --> 00:42:55,239
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority,</i>

646
00:42:55,940 --> 00:42:57,241
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

647
00:42:57,841 --> 00:43:01,979
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

648
00:43:03,180 --> 00:43:05,683
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

649
00:43:06,283 --> 00:43:07,318
<i>Also known as...</i>

650
00:43:08,218 --> 00:43:09,687
<i>Doctor X.</i>

651
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:14,925
Who the hell is Michiko Daimon?

652
00:43:16,560 --> 00:43:19,463
She volunteers
to take operations for money,

653
00:43:19,530 --> 00:43:21,231
no matter the risks to the patient.

654
00:43:22,032 --> 00:43:23,601
She's a dirty mercenary.

655
00:43:24,802 --> 00:43:25,636
I found it.

656
00:43:26,203 --> 00:43:28,439
This is the procedure Daimon used.

657
00:43:29,974 --> 00:43:31,375
April 2005.

658
00:43:32,309 --> 00:43:34,445
The gastrointestinal surgery team

659
00:43:34,511 --> 00:43:36,981
at the Cubanancan Medical
University Hospital in Cuba,

660
00:43:37,047 --> 00:43:42,553
succeeded in a vascular graft surgery
of the superior mesenteric artery

661
00:43:43,187 --> 00:43:48,626
<i>and brought the hope</i>
<i>of a complete cure to the patient.</i>

662
00:43:49,326 --> 00:43:52,730
<i>However, the patient died</i>
<i>one month after the surgery.</i>

663
00:43:54,865 --> 00:43:57,001
The cause of death
has not been made clear.

664
00:44:01,005 --> 00:44:03,807
The name of the primary surgeon
recorded on the medical record is...

665
00:44:10,914 --> 00:44:12,316
<i>Doctor X.</i>

666
00:45:45,542 --> 00:45:46,677
This drama is fiction. All names of people
and organizations are fictional.

667
00:45:46,777 --> 00:45:47,811
Medical practices in the drama vary
depending on a person's medical condition.

668
00:45:47,878 --> 00:45:48,879
Subtitle translation by Paul Koehler

669
00:45:48,946 --> 00:45:49,780
NEXT EPISODE

670
00:45:49,847 --> 00:45:51,515
I will not fail.

671
00:45:51,582 --> 00:45:52,850
IF SHE OPERATES, WILL SHE BE SUED?

672
00:45:52,916 --> 00:45:55,552
Some illnesses can't be cured!
If you get sued, that's fine!

673
00:45:55,619 --> 00:45:57,121
Daimon, you will take responsibility.

674
00:45:57,187 --> 00:45:58,288
FREELANCE DOCTOR VS. MONSTER PATIENT

675
00:45:58,355 --> 00:46:00,023
<i>Shouldn't someone else apologize?</i>

676
00:46:00,190 --> 00:46:01,391
<i>Don't say that to the family!</i>

677
00:46:01,458 --> 00:46:03,527
While you say that, the patient will die!
